# QNX Screen configuration for "real_graphics" environments (docs/REAL_GRAPHICS.md). IDEmu's builder writes it to the shim
# disk as realgfx/graphics.conf, with {width} and {height} set to the environment's display.
#
# It is the firmware's own lib/graphics/omap5430_ES2_0/graphics-<width>_<height>.conf cut down to what runs without the
# GPUs: QEMU models the OMAP5430 display controller (DSS) but neither the PowerVR SGX540 nor the Vivante GC320.
#  - EGL display 1 keeps the firmware's SGX library lists, so Screen's clients load as on the car, but not its kernel
#    driver (gpu-dlls): EGL/GLES cannot initialise. IDEmu's HMI path keeps drawing through glhost.
#  - EGL display 2 (the GC320 blitter) is left out; Screen composes with its software blitter (blit-config and usage sw).
#  - WFD device 1 is the real OMAP5430 driver, with only the GFX pipeline bound to display 1. The firmware's video
#    pipelines, its second display and its MFLAG, extproc and GC320 memory settings are left out.
begin khronos
    begin egl display 1
        egl-dlls = [IMG%s] libusc.so libsrv_um.so libpvr2d.so libIMGegl.so
        glesv1-dlls = libusc.so libsrv_um.so libIMGegl.so libImgGLESv1_CM.so
        glesv2-dlls = libusc.so libsrv_um.so libusc.so libIMGegl.so libImgGLESv2.so
        gpu-string = SGX540rev120
        aperture = 250
    end egl display

    begin wfd device 1
        wfd-dlls = libwfdcfg.so libWFDomap5430ES2_0.so
        gfx = 1
    end wfd device
end khronos

begin winmgr
    begin globals
        blit-config = sw
    end globals
    begin display 1
        formats = rgba8888 rgbx8888
        video-mode = {width} x {height} @ 60
    end display
    begin class framebuffer1
        display = 1
        pipeline = 4
        format = rgba8888
        usage = sw
    end class
end winmgr
